are preserved at the top of each extracted source file. The pinned source
distribution has LICENSE.txt and no separate NOTICE file. Its Apache License
2.0 is copied without modification to licenses/LICENSE.NLTK. The historical
LICENSE.TXT references in the unchanged source headers refer to that copy.

MODIFICATIONS: mifolyo's Indexer maintainers selected inference-only source,
removed unused APIs and imports, removed TokenizerI inheritance, fixed the Punkt
constructor to supplied parameters and default English language/token classes,
and retained only the default NLTKWordTokenizer execution path. No inference
regex or decision rule was rewritten. The fixed-path verified loader and public
wrapper are local code; its zero-on-miss orthographic table does not retain new
words encountered in input. The extraction selections and adaptations are in
tools/vendor_nlp.py (relative to services/indexer) and component.json.

DATA NOT CHECKED INTO GIT: English punkt_tab and stopwords data are from nltk_data
commit 550b6625bcef1f2abff2ff770a5a0d272c9c6b2a. Their redistribution license
is NOT established. Both are explicitly listed as unclarified/unknown in the
pinned upstream DATASET-LICENSES.md. No data license is invented or inferred
from NLTK's Apache license or the mifolyo repository's MIT license.

The project owner explicitly approved pinned/hash-verified private build/test
provisioning and offline runtime, with corpus bytes kept OUT of Git. That project
workflow approval is NOT legal clearance or permission to publish data/images.
Data-bearing images/artifacts must remain private. Redistribution review remains
unresolved; the separate --distribution verifier gate blocks publication even
when all source/asset integrity checks pass. The public data index identity and
its two relevant package metadata records are pinned in provenance/data-index.json.

The pinned nltk_data repository license is retained in licenses/LICENSE.nltk_data
for its licensing documentation copied under provenance/. That repository-wide
license does NOT resolve the individual data package licenses. See the exact
upstream provenance/LICENSE-OVERVIEW.md and provenance/DATASET-LICENSES.md.

This is not a full NLTK distribution, an upstream security release, or a package
that pip-audit inspects. Keep the normal dependency audit unchanged, and review
this separately maintained source component and upstream advisories as well.
